{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"     163 /Users/evintunador/.claude/jobs/6059dc80/tmp/gen_inference_log.txt\ncommit f046c55bf303a5c208c824d5fd58a6e519df6327\nAuthor: evintunador <evintunador@gmail.com>\nDate:   Wed Mar 25 23:58:47 2026 +0000\n\n    fix(gen): sample from correct logit position + prevent double EOS\n    \n    Two bugs fixed in _generate_doc:\n    \n    1. Logit position: was always sampling from logits[0, -1, :] (last\n       position in packed sequence). When generating an aux doc inserted\n       before root, position -1 is root's last token — aux docs got tokens\n       sampled from root's distribution. Now finds the entry's span end\n       from doc_spans and samples from logits[0, span_end-1, :].\n    \n    2. Double EOS: when a layout policy provides a suffix starting with EOS\n       (e.g. BOSEOSLayoutPolicy), the generated EOS was appended to the body\n       AND mark_done added it again as suffix, producing a double EOS never\n       seen during training. Now detects this case and skips body append.\n    \n    Port of _layout_suffix_starts_with helper from main worktree.\n    \n    Updated ScriptedModel to place target tokens at the correct per-document\n    logit positions (matching the new sampling behavior). Added 3 new tests:\n    - double EOS prevention with layout suffix\n    - EOS appended normally without layout\n    - aux doc sampled from correct logit position (not root's)\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n model/generation_loop.py       |  45 +++++++++++-\n tests/model/test_generation.py | 155 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----\n 2 files changed, 181 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)\n\ncommit dcd2d6e468da12dbbfe4c38a1fddf936ca9448cc\nAuthor: evintunador <evintunador@gmail.com>\nDate:   Wed Mar 25 22:44:01 2026 +0000\n\n    test(gen): integration tests for re-eviction, trace, and multi-step scenarios\n    \n    A