ross FQN-colliding namespaces.\n251\t\n252\t## REVIEWER-ATTACKABLE\n253\t1. Rungs independent not nested (resampling vs scale; noise floor not quantified beyond single-ckpt bootstrap CI).\n254\t2. Only 2 REAL rungs (3.9B, 8B); 16B broken → \"does lead grow?\" unanswered; FLAT claim rests on 2 points.\n255\t3. Specialist baselines HETEROGENEOUS (kotlin/ts external ports ASE/CrossCodeEval vs merge internal ports; go/rust/js no external baseline) → 2.8×/11× indicative not exact.\n256\t4. **Within-source packing → cross-source edges NEVER trained on.** Merged graph HAS cross-source edges but packs strictly within-source. \"11 link types together\" = interleaved within-source packs sharing params = MULTI-TASK MIXING not cross-modality attention within a pack. STATE explicitly to preempt.\n257\t5. doc_causal-arm control ports still TODO (should show ≈0 Δ); placebo-separation is current stand-in.\n258\t6. Composite single-lang-per-doc + generation content-sniff mis-class degrade silently (only qualitative gen).\n259\t7. wiki REGRESSED on ppl (6.64→6.79) lone source worse — unexplained negative transfer.\n260\t8. LR/WD never retuned for larger rungs; broken 16B = evidence recipe doesn't transfer across scale, undercuts \"only variable is diversity\" at scale.\n261\tFLAGS: epoch_16b_natural recipe (no script); cross-source co-packing (code implies never); exact 8B per-source pack counts.\n262\t\n263\t## → LIT REVIEW IMPLICATIONS\n264\t- Multi-task / multi-domain LM training; data mixing / domain weighting (DoReMi, data mixture laws).\n265\t- Multilingual + multi-domain transfer; negative transfer / interference.\n266\t- Multi-epoch training / data-constrained scaling (Muennighoff 2-4 epochs) [have].\n267\t- Curriculum / balanced sampling across sources.\n268\t<!-- PROVENANCE\n269\tWritten against commit 6134163 (main @ 2026-08-07). This brief describes the code as of\n270\tthat commit; it is NOT authoritative if the source has changed since. Before trusting it,\n271\tcheck whether the covered sources have drifted:\n272\t    git diff --stat 6134163..HEAD -- kernels/\n273\tEmpty output = brief still current. Non-empty = re-verify the changed parts against source.\n274\tCovered sources: kernels/\n275\t-->\n276\t\n277\t# CODE BRIEF: Triton attention kernels (agent a0332a4a)\n278\tKERNELS.md STALE (says v12 prod); ground truth = triton_v18 (cross-doc), varlen_bim_v2 (doc-causal) per CLAUDE.md + attention.py:199-229. Both wrap v10 core.\n279\t\n280\t## BIM = Block Interaction Mask (BlockInteractionMask, cross_doc_mask.py:69-144)\n281\tPrecomputed block-level CSR (Q-block,KV-block)→interact?, \"analogous to FlexAttn BlockMask WITHOUT B/H dims\" (mask same across all heads+layers → built ONCE per batch, reused). Two reps:\n282\t- Grant bitmasks: grant k→chunk k//64 bit k%64, [n_chunks,T] int64 q/kv; in_grant=any_c((q_bm[c,i]&kv_bm[c,j])!=0), pointwise no seq reduction. 512KB@32k vs ~1GB dense. bit63=INT64_MIN. kernel OR-over-chunks = tl.static_range unrolled.\n283\t- BIM/CSR block table (_build_block_interaction_mask:597-914): CPU numpy ~1-2ms/batch, OR-reduce bitmasks to block granularity, emit q_kv_* (fwd + dQ bwd) + kv_q_* (dK/dV bwd) CSR. Grid (n_blocks,H), each CTA walks only its CSR row → empty pairs never launched. bim.sparsity = fraction causal pairs skipped.\n284\t- CSR ORDERED BY BLOCK CLASS → progressively cheaper inner loops: FULL (single-doc same-doc off-diag, NO masking), PURE_CROSS (v13: single-doc diff-doc, bitmask-only no doc_id load), BOUNDARY (straddles, full same_doc|in_grant), DIAGONAL (full+causal). Order [full,pure_cross,boundary,diagonal].\n285\t- Ordinal run-index relabel (:636-669): same-doc block-overlap test needs monotonic labels; traversal-order doc_ids NON-monotonic; relabel cumsum(doc-id changes). Without it: straddling block drops same-doc KV → softmax collapse → NaN/dQ~5.7e4 in thestack cross_doc_link training. CITE as correctness fix.\n286\t\n287\t## Speed vs FlexAttention (A100 80GB bf16, 16h Dh64 doc512; KERNELS.md:16-49)\n288\tv12: T=4k 0.91×, T=32k 0.77× total (fwd 2× faster 1.14 vs 2.38ms, bwd 12% 5.52 vs 6.30ms). **Dh=128: FlexAttn bwd COLLAPSES to 177ms → v12/v18 bwd 16.85ms ~9-10× faster.** varlen_bim_v2 targets vslf-class (old triton_varlen 31ms fwd vs vslf 0.54ms; vslf bwd unusable on real packed data) — BIM gets vslf-class fwd WITH reliable gradients.\n289\tWhy faster: (1) v10 native bf16 TC matmuls, no fp32 load, post-mult scale → half register/SMEM → higher occupancy; (2) v11 no permute/contiguous, THD layout direct strides → -200MB HBM/step@32k, peak 271/340→69/138MB (flex parity) +0.35ms fwd; (3) v12 BIM_BLOCK_SIZE=128 larger bwd tiles; (4) structural: precompute block schedule once/batch, specialize per class, no empty-block launch, no per-block mask re-eval.\n290\t\n291\t## Varlen (packed) handling\n292\tLegacy varlen_attn.py slow. Production varlen_bim_v2: reuse BIM CSR for PURE doc-causal (grants all-zero), inner kernels check only same_doc+causal, ZERO bitmask loads; off-diag same-doc blocks→full fast path, only diagonal masked. BIM cached by (id(cu_seqlens|doc_ids),seq_len). _from_doc_ids entry handles non-contiguous doc spans + doc_id=-1 gaps.\n293\t\n294\t## fused_relu_sq_mlp + polar_express\n295\t- fused squared-ReLU MLP: out=relu(x@W1ᵀ)²@W2, one Triton matmul fp32 grouped-swizzle L2, mode-switched epilogue (fwd save pre-act; bwd (grad@W2ᵀ)·2·relu(pre)); W2 stored TRANSPOSED (no .T.contiguous in bwd), zero-init (muP). fp32 activation. layer.py:47.\n296\t- polar_express: Muon orthogonalization REPLACING Newton-Schulz, arXiv:2505.16932. Per-iter tuned coeffs (5 iters). a·X+(b·A+c·A²)·X via 3 custom Triton kernels XXT/XTX/ba_plus_cAA exploiting SYMMETRY (skip ~half tiles + mirror-store). Picks XᵀX vs XXᵀ by tall/wide. Fuses Nesterov(fp32)+orthog(bf16) in one torch.compile. Spectral-norm 2e-2 margin. momentum_t 0-D CPU tensor (avoid recompile). H100-autotuned, functional-not-optimal on A100. [DUP w/ muon brief]\n297\t\n298\t## Autotuning\n299\t@triton.autotune narrow hand-curated grids keyed [N,Dh,n_chunks,BIM_BLOCK_SIZE]; fwd 24 configs (KV{32,64}×stages{3,4,5}×warps{4,8}); bwd MICRO{16,32,64} (128 excluded so BS64%MICRO==0). EXPANDING grid was REGRESSION (v14 noisy single-run autotuner false-picked degenerate MICRO=128). .autotune_cache.json persists kernel→config, bypasses search (concurrent multi-rank JIT autotune corrupts compiler).\n300\t\n301\t## Novel/publishable\n302\t- BIM: layer/head-shared block-class-partitioned CSR schedule for structured cross-doc masks. Amortize O((T/bs)²) CPU precompute over all layers/heads + per-class dispatch. Genuinely novel vs FlexAttn per-call block-mask eval.\n303\t- Bitmask grant encoding O(T) not O(T²), no seq reduction, + block-level OR-union prune.\n304\t- Ordinal run-index relabel (correctness fix tied to real NaN).\n305\t- Asymmetric fwd(128)/bwd(64) block sizes (v17/18) for A100 SMEM@Dh128 → ~2× bwd.\n306\t- Sentinel-LSE NaN guard (v18): flash M=-1e6 sentinel survives for tokens w/ zero valid KV → exp2(+1e6)=inf, inf×0=NaN; fixed post-kernel nan_to_num (zero fwd output anyway). Publishable numerical-stability finding for sparse-mask flash attn.\n307\t- Documented dead-ends v5-v9 + failed v14-v16 w/ root cause (rigorous negatives).\n308\t- fused sq-ReLU MLP + symmetric-matmul Polar Express = solid eng (methods themselves prior work).\n309\t\n310\tFLAGS: KERNELS.md stale (trust code); v18 exact ratio not cleanly re-benched (v18=v17+NaN guard); varlen 31/0.54/2.3× author-reported docstring; NO GPU run (all numbers as-documented).\n311\t\n312\t## → LIT REVIEW IMPLICATIONS\n313\t- A6 kernel slice: Triton (Tillet), FlashAttention kernel design, block-sparse GPU kernels, online softmax (Milakov flash-attn precursor), bitmask/CSR sparse attention.\n314\t- Numerical stability of softmax/flash under full masking → could cite.\n315\t","tool_use_id":"toolu_012RkME2q26TfQUTbPjuDFRj","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repo