e suspect)\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 5cbbe416-90e8-4a21-93e7-044acf862880\n  modified: 2026-08-24T03:56:16.552Z\n---\n\nDecisions for `paper/` made 2026-08-23 (not derivable from code):\n\n- **Main thesis** is that `cross_doc_link` *maintains causality* so a model learns from\n  plain pretraining that emitting a reference opens access to it → native cross-doc\n  generation / corpus-fetching with no SFT/RL. This is UNMEASURED (models too small to\n  generate coherently); the paper states it as the central open measurement (§1, §7, §8).\n- **Sparsity/density scaling law** (solo models, unaffected by the merged retraction) is\n  IN the paper as a finding about *capability/intelligence* (inference-time density\n  dominates; dc-trained model reads a handed target nearly as well). It must NOT be\n  presented as evidence for/against the thesis above.\n- **arXiv is scoped out**: 32k window holds 1–2 papers/pack, so targets are rarely\n  co-packed; the arXiv sweep is uninformative until sequence-parallel training exists.\n- **Wiki community_pack negative** (RESULTS_graph_sparsity §4): Evin suspects harness\n  corruption; paper makes NO claim about generic held-out wiki text until audited.\n  HotpotQA (+1.29) stays the wiki headline.\n- **HotpotQA placebo** may already be implemented in an unpushed worktree on fss.\n- Author line: Evin Tunador, HOPPR.\n\n**How to apply:** when editing the paper, keep these three things separate (thesis /\ncapability finding / scoped-out modality) and don't re-ask. Cluster-side follow-ups are\nin TODOS.md \"Paper — cluster-reliant items\". Related: [[provenance-from-laptop]].\n","filePath":"/Users/evintunador/.claude/projects/-Users-evintunador-repos-evintunador-tagseq2tagseq/memory/paper-framing-2026-08-23.md","memdirStamped":true,"originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[],"type":"create","userModified":false},"type":"user","userType":"external","uuid":"b554c7f9-3b56-4236-9b1a-fe2fa5e37596","version":