ph} under graph (bfs/dfs) packing versus"," \\val{traversal.wiki_val_loss.random} under random packing. The incremental","-cross-document benefit is itself traversal-robust: the Wikipedia HotpotQA","-$\\Delta\\mathrm{nll}$ is \\val{crossdoc.wiki_hotpotqa.dfs.delta_nll} (dfs),","-\\val{crossdoc.wiki_hotpotqa.rw.delta_nll} (random walk), and","-\\val{crossdoc.wiki_hotpotqa.random.delta_nll} (random) against the bfs headline above,","-and the Java cross-document $\\Delta\\mathrm{nll}$ stays positive across all four","-traversals (\\Cref{tab:traversal}). Packing quality and cross-document attention are two","-decoupled axes: traversal strongly moves base-model loss and only weakly moves the","-within-model cross-document gain.","+cross-document benefit is itself traversal-robust --- every Wikipedia and Java arm of","+\\Cref{tab:traversal} is positive, with random packing the weakest --- so packing","+quality and cross-document attention are two decoupled axes: traversal strongly moves","+base-model loss and only weakly moves the within-model cross-document gain."," % The two validation-loss figures are read from training logs, not the eval harness, and"," % are tracked as grounding debt until a log-value source lands; see provenance/README.md.","-% The dfs/rw/random HotpotQA arms were scored at n=377 (max_grants=256 re-eval); the bfs","-% headline at n=738. Table in App. Z shows n per row."," "," \\subsection{The cross-document benefit scales with realized link density}"," \\label{sec:results:density}"],"newLines":120,"newStart":15,"oldLines":69,"oldStart":15},{"lines":[" per pack (out-degree $\\times$ co-packing rate $\\times\\kappa$) yields a single"," cross-dataset line with correlation \\fillin{$r$, eval-time, code} over"," \\fillin{$n$} points and slope \\fillin{nats per realized grant}, extrapolating above","-today's densest corpus. Raw graph out-degree is the wrong axis (\\fillin{$r$, out-degree}):","-it counts edges whose targets are never co-packed and hence never attended.","+today's densest corpus. Raw graph out-degree is the wrong axis, with correlation","+\\fillin{$r$, out-degree}: it counts edges whose targets are never co-packed and hence","+never attended."," "," Retraining at each $\\kappa$ and re-evaluating at full density gives the train-time"," line, which is monotone but strongly \\emph{concave}: most of the benefit is already"],"newLines":9,"newStart":142,"oldLines":8,"oldStart":91},{"lines":[" % (14.2), go +0.003 (5.4), java ~0 (3.1), zig -0.007 (5.1); 2D grid eval-axis swing"," % ~0.04-0.05 vs train-axis ~0.005; keep0-row TS dc-trained +0.041 vs cdl-trained +0.040"," % (preliminary; full 6-dataset row was SLURM 81104). Ground via a provenance `artifact`","-% source kind (TODOS.md). Figures: sparsity_scaling/fig_sparsity.png, fig_traintime.png,","-% fig_grid2d.png, regression.png -- copy into paper/figures/ once grounded.","+% source kind (TODOS.md); add a per-dataset Δ@κ table + the regression figure here once","+% grounded. Figures: sparsity_scaling/fig_sparsity.png, fig_traintime.png, fig_grid2d.png,","+% regression.png -- copy into paper/figures/."," "," \\subsection{Diversity scaling (merged multi-source model)}"," \\label{sec:results:diversity}"],"newLines":9,"newStart":172,"oldLines":8,"oldStart":120},{"lines":[" % BUT the entire merged_all_v2 family was retracted 2026-08-14 (sequential-not-interleaved"," % dataloader bug; see RESULTS_graph_sparsity.md) and this claim is built on it. Kotlin/TS"," % baselines are external ports (indicative, not exact). Re-run on a fixed merge before grounding.","+% Add the per-port merge-vs-specialist table here once re-run."," "," \\subsection{Density-aware scheduling efficiency}"," \\label{sec:results:efficiency}","-Density-aware batching yields a \\fillin{mean $\\times$} mean / \\fillin{max $\\times$} max","-step-time \\fillin{speedup/slowdown?} over live training with online link detection and","-random density assignment, with within-bucket step-time coefficient of variation","-\\fillin{$\\downarrow$/$\\uparrow$?} (\\Cref{fig:density-timing}). Part of the mean gain is","-the removal of online link detection from the step and part is the removal of the","-rank stall; the latter is most visible across nodes and near zero on a single NVLink","-node.","-% Wall-clock timing (step_timing_rank*.csv), not the eval harness. Raw CSVs are not located","-% in-repo and carry no run_id; only README.md prose + docs/images/density_aware_timing*.png","-% survive. Indicative only until the originating run + its CSVs are identified.","+Precomputing packs and scheduling by density buys wall-clock time twice: link","+detection leaves the training step, and no rank stalls at the all-reduce waiting for a","+denser pack. Measured on a two-node, two-GPUs-per-node run on The Stack at $32$k","+context (\\Cref{tab:efficiency}), mean step time drops from","+\\val{efficiency.step_time.live_mean}\\,s to \\val{efficiency.step_time.precomputed_mean}\\,s","+(a \\val{efficiency.speedup_mean}$\\times$ speedup) and worst-case step time from","+\\val{efficiency.step_time.live_max}\\,s to \\val{efficiency.step_time.precomputed_max}\\,s","+(\\val{efficiency.speedup_max}$\\times$). The live path's step-time distribution is broad","+and structureless (coefficient of variation \\val{efficiency.cov.live}\\%), while under","+density bucketing the within-bucket variation collapses to a mean of","+\\val{efficiency.cov.precomputed_within_bucket}\\% --- the remaining spread is","+\\emph{between} buckets, deterministic and density-driven (\\Cref{fig:density-timing}).","+The rank-stall component is most visible across nodes and near zero on a single","+NVLink node.","+% Grounding status: these figures are ledger LITERALS (efficiency.*) copied from","+% README.md \"Measured impact\"; the step_timing_rank*.csv files are not located in-repo","+% and carry no run_id. Tracked as grounding debt; replace with a kind:artifact source","+% once the originating run (or a re-timing at the same layout) lands. See TODOS.md."," ","+\\begin{table}[t]","+  \\centering","+  \\small","+  \\begin{tabular}{@{}lrrr@{}}","+    \\toprule","+    & Live & Precomputed, density-bucketed & Speedup \\\\","+    \\midrule","+    Mean step time & \\val{efficiency.step_time.live_mean}\\,s & \\val{efficiency.step_time.precomputed_mean}\\,s & \\val{efficiency.speedup_mean}$\\times$ \\\\","+    Max step time  & \\val{efficiency.step_time.live_max}\\,s  & \\val{efficiency.step_time.precomputed_max}\\,s  & \\val{efficiency.speedup_max}$\\times$ \\\\","+    Step-time CoV  & \\val{efficiency.cov.live}\\%             & \\val{efficiency.cov.precomputed_within_bucket}\\% within-bucket & \\\\","+    \\bottomrule","+  \\end{tabular}","+  \\caption{Wall-clock effect of density-aware scheduling ($2$ nodes $\\times$ $2$ GPUs,","+  The Stack, $32$k context). ``Live'' traverses the graph, detects links, and builds","+  the mask online with random pack-to-rank assignment; ``precomputed'' uses offline","+  packs and draws every rank's pack from the same density bucket at each step.}","+  \\label{tab:efficiency}","+\\end{table}","+"," \\begin{figure}[t]","   \\centering","   \\includegraphics[width=\\linewidth]{density_aware_timing.png}"],"newLines":48,"newStart":187,"oldLines":20,"oldStart":134}],"type":"update","userModified":false},"type":"user","userType":"external","uuid":"359a4b70-3565-45c5-95b2-3942110fdc82","version":"2.1.241"},"format":"claude-code-jsonl/1"},"recorded_at":"2026-08-26T16:12:08.214Z","schema":"conversation-ledger/v1"}
