{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"let's do your suggested 1-3, 5-6 and make sure all the cluster-reliant stuff is in our todos\nthen for your questions:\n1. yeah i need to go back and look at the specifics here; i'm suspicious that that community_pack finding is corrupted\n2. yeah we likely have to pull back from arxiv. teh reality is that arxiv docs are very long and we only have a sequence length of 32k so most packs were only 1 or 2 documents, making that whole analysis useless until i can implement sequence-parallel\n3. that is a sharp finding about _intelligence_ and should be included. however, it does not speak to the real benefit of cross-doc-link which is _maintaining causality_ in a manner that makes native cross-doc genration/corpus-fetching possible from only pre-training, no SSFT/RL/etc, which i suspect will be our main finding and we've yet to actually measure, partly because these models are so tiny that they're not legitimately smart enough to do reasonably intelligent generation, but i do need to figure out how to measure that given our constraints; pls add to the todos as well\n4. i think i may have fixed this in a local worktree on fss but forgotten to push; leave as a tentative todo pls\n5. should be, might not have been added tho\n6. Evin Tunador, affiliation HOPPR","type":"text"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/tagseq2tagseq","dirty_fingerprint":"eb66eb2dce29bf19de8230295a45870e6fee8471808fbd0ce44a344536bce2b2","head":"5c15f9d0ec9630286ce8d7d66c05e849ae72097f","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/tagseq2tagseq.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:5cbbe416-90e8-4a21-93e7-044acf862880","seq":135},"id":"ev1-5692e9b6aad7b04bf1cfbf474028478665a51971720b725b3f27b24e634432e8","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-24T03:32:58.261Z","producer":{"session_id":"5cbbe416-90e8-4a21-93e7-044acf862880","source":"claude